{% block brandDescription %}
      <p class="brand-description">Founded in 1980 by Grover Jackson, Jackson Guitars emerged from a California repair shop to define the "shred" guitar era, heavily influenced by a custom collaboration with Randy Rhoads. Known for high-performance features like compound radius fretboards, "hot" pickups, and sharp, angular bodies (Rhoads, Soloist, King V, Dinky, Kelly), the company became synonymous with 1980s heavy metal. Acquired by Fender in 2002, Jackson continues to produce iconic instruments for metal and hard rock.<br><a href="#" class="decoder-howto-link" data-modal-target="howto-jackson">(How to decode a Jackson serial #)</a></p>
